// Planting Intelligence · design journey. Describe (Imagine) → Shape (site model + AI planting-bed proposal, editable) →
// Compose (intent, per-bed candidates) → Grow (generate, explore, revise, export). One model (model.js), one knowledge adapter
// over brain/data/explorer.json (knowledge.js), one interpreter (intent.js: offline rules; a live model through
// tools/design_server.py when configured), the spatial proposal engine (spatial.js over clip.js), one planting engine (engine.js),
// the 2D renderer (render.js) and the 3D garden (garden3d.js). Every view reads the same state S and the same project; every
// change goes through the model, so plan, garden, schedule, exports and the saved file agree. The Imagine stage (hero, art,
// composer) keeps its artwork and motion; V4 (2026-11-15) reduced the landing to one invitation, added the Objective panel, the
// "what changed" note and the preview / generated-version naming (see design/css/v4.css and platform/js/trace.js).
